      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Visual hallucinations may be caused by organic cerebral lesions and by drugs including indomethacin. We report here a case of indomethacin-induced visual hallucinations in which a clear description of the phenomenology shows how a complex hallucinatory experience may arise from the relatively non-specific effects of cerebral irritation."},
